## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  redactionVersion: string;
  implicatedRegions: string[];
  tenantIds: string[];
  severity: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the effectiveness of the redaction rollback in production?
- Which metrics would you surface to product and compliance teams during a breach incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of drift in a multi-tenant streaming system with region isolation, ensuring containment without collateral impact. It also probes data lineage, governance, and rollout discipline.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with tenant scope, region, evidence, ownership, and lineage
- Region-tenant gated lifecycle to prevent cross-tenant bleed
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked logs/traces
- Tenant-scoped metrics: containment MTTR, drift score, recurrence rate, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollback plan for sessionization logic changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: CAPA data model (conceptual)
class CAPA {
  constructor(id, tenantId, region) {
    this.id = id;
    this.tenantId = tenantId;
    this.region = region;
    this.evidence = [];
    this.rootCause = null;
    this.actions = [];
    this.owner = null;
    this.state = 'DETECTED';
    this.timestamps = {};
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test isolation between tenants during a canary rollout?
- How would you handle cross-tenant drift if tenants share resources?

